COPIED from the re-review's scratch (.build/review-wp207 of the supervisor's workspace) at WP-211's merge, unchanged, so the
measurements spec/incr.md cites stay runnable. The absolute paths below and inside gnu-warning.sh and ar-flips.sh
(lines 7-8) are that scratch's: set them to a scratch directory of your own before running those two. The four
Python scripts take their paths as arguments.

R-2 (WP-208) scratch: the re-review of WP-207's second design pass of the
incremental update. Report: briefs/reviews/review-wp207.md. Everything here
is mine; nothing of mine lives elsewhere. Run each script from any directory
with absolute paths, as below. Python 3, GNU toolchain (gcc, ld.bfd), and for
gnu-warning.sh the mortar `ld` shim of .build/review-in72/bin (read-only).

extract_mine.py [PROGRAMS]          (default 3000; the report used 1000)
  My own model of resolve.md 4.1 (closure from scratch) and of incr.md
  IN-71b, written from their text, in two readings of "lazy" (archive member
  / FILES LAZY flag). Named cases R1a, R1b, R2-1 (round shortcut) and a
  random series of 4 hops per program; also compares the stored ROUND with
  the full link's breadth-first round (IN-78 lists round as "computed afresh").
    python3 /Volumes/AgentWork/mortar-helper/.build/review-wp207/extract_mine.py 1000 \
      > /Volumes/AgentWork/mortar-helper/.build/review-wp207/extract_mine.out
  ~1 minute.

ar-flips.sh
  GNU ld -t -t member sets of a static AArch64 link for one-line source edits
  (c0..c2: C; x0..x4: C++: iostream, thread, to_string, regex); counts members
  flipped and their defined globals. Work files in ar/. Output: ar-flips.out.
    /Volumes/AgentWork/mortar-helper/.build/review-wp207/ar-flips.sh \
      > /Volumes/AgentWork/mortar-helper/.build/review-wp207/ar-flips.out
  ~1 minute (gcc/g++ -O1 -static, 8 links).

syncprobe.py DIR [MB] [ROUNDS]
  The fixed cost of IN-77's W1..W6 plus the lock round trip, on DIR's file
  system, 50 MB output, 9 MB state, 4 dirty 1 MiB windows. Creates and removes
  DIR/out.bin, DIR/.out.bin.mortar-torn, DIR/out.bin.mortar-state. DIR must
  exist (virtiofs: a directory under .build/review-wp207; overlay: a
  `mktemp -d` removed afterwards by its literal printed path).
    python3 /Volumes/AgentWork/mortar-helper/.build/review-wp207/syncprobe.py <DIR> 50 15

aside.py DIR
  IN-77's aside name: (1) exec of P while U1's O_RDWR descriptor is open
  (ETXTBSY); (2) W4's rename(A, P) over a foreign file a plain link put at P;
  (3) link(A, P) gives EEXIST instead; (3b) link+unlink leaves nlink 1.
  Creates and removes DIR/out and DIR/.out.mortar-torn.
    python3 /Volumes/AgentWork/mortar-helper/.build/review-wp207/aside.py <DIR>

gnu-warning.sh
  IN-75a's subject: glibc's .gnu.warning.mktemp (an UNCHANGED libc.a member)
  produces a warning whose existence and text ("referenced by c.o:(.text+0x24)")
  are decided by the CHANGED file c.o. Mortar (full links, incremental mode)
  and GNU ld, v1 -> v2 -> v1. Work files and logs in gw/.
    /Volumes/AgentWork/mortar-helper/.build/review-wp207/gnu-warning.sh

region_day.py [SEED] [HOPS]
  My own model of IN-72 item 2 (keep / grow in place / first fit / overflow
  region) and item 3 (tail reserve, growth step) over a "day" of 200 random
  one-function edits on abstract .text-only files; 40 and 400 files, one or
  ten files edited, 10 seeds each. Output: region_day.out. ~10 s.
    python3 /Volumes/AgentWork/mortar-helper/.build/review-wp207/region_day.py 1 200 \
      > /Volumes/AgentWork/mortar-helper/.build/review-wp207/region_day.out

Removal: find /Volumes/AgentWork/mortar-helper/.build/review-wp207 -mindepth 1 -delete
